* ===========================================================================
*  CP/M-over-serial, increment 2: serial CONSOLE routines in MOL80.
*
*  First real MOL80 source file (assembled by mol80asm, committed to the repo).
*  Reproduces the serial sign-on + echo demo, written in MOL80, exercising the
*  confirmed PORT(n) I/O and the ORG/DB/DS directives.
*
*  Serial port (MachineConfig defaults; [VERIFY] vs. real CPT hardware):
*     DATA   = port 112 (70H)  -- received byte in / transmit byte out
*     STATUS = port 113 (71H)  -- bit 0 = RX ready, bit 1 = TX ready
*
*  Full-line comments begin with '*' (our-convention placeholder). Code lines
*  are kept free of inline comments to avoid column counting.
* ===========================================================================
          ORG 0
*
*  Entry: set up a stack, print the sign-on, then echo forever.
START     STACK:HL
          HL:SP
          MSG:HL
          CALL(PRINT)
ECHO      CALL(CONIN)
          CALL(CONOUT)
          /ECHO
*
*  CONOUT: send the byte in A out the serial port (wait for TX ready).
*  Stash A on the stack across the status poll (the poll clobbers A).
CONOUT    PSW:STK
COWAIT    PORT(113):A
          A+*2:A
          FZ=1? /COWAIT
          STK:PSW
          A:PORT(112)
          RTN
*
*  CONIN: wait for a received byte, return it in A.
CONIN     PORT(113):A
          A+*1:A
          FZ=1? /CONIN
          PORT(112):A
          RTN
*
*  PRINT: send the NUL-terminated string at HL.
PRINT     (HL):A
          A+*255:A
          FZ=1? /PDONE
          CALL(CONOUT)
          HL+1:HL
          /PRINT
PDONE     RTN
*
*  Data: sign-on message, NUL-terminated.
MSG       DB "CPT serial demo (MOL80) online.", 13, 10
          DB "Type and it echoes:", 13, 10, 0
*
*  Stack: reserve space; SP starts at STACK (top, grows down).
          DS 32
STACK     DS 0
